# `.rx/gotchas.md` is an append-only log — every agent appends its lesson at EOF.
# Two agents branching from the same base therefore collide there every single
# time, even though their entries are semantically independent. `merge=union`
# keeps both sides instead of raising a conflict. (ENG-1012)
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to `.rx/guardrails.md` or `.rx/mockups.md`: those hold
# rules and references that agents EDIT rather than append to. Union is dumb — on
# an edited line it silently keeps BOTH versions rather than asking a human, which
# for a guardrail would mean two contradictory rules shipping unnoticed. A conflict
# in those files is the correct outcome, so they stay unmanaged.
#
# The same caveat applies here in the rare case two agents edit the SAME existing
# gotchas entry: both rewrites survive, adjacent. For an append-only log that is
# visible and harmless; for a rule file it would not be.
.rx/gotchas.md merge=union
